# Anisotropy

Nothing enters the game below the GPU's max anisotropy.

- Use `installMaxAnisotropy` in `js/anisotropy.js`. It runs on every texture created after the renderer exists, including textures inside loaded models.
- Do not cap anisotropy. Do not hardcode a lower number.
- Do not turn mipmaps off, and do not use `NearestFilter`, to skip this.
- Skip only textures where anisotropy has no effect: no mipmaps, `NearestFilter`, render targets, and shadow maps. Do not change their filters.
